<article class="env-lemma" id="04E9">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04E9">Lemma <span data-tag="04E9">10.148.5</span>.</a> Let $A \to B$ be a formally unramified ring map. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
For $S \subset A$ a multiplicative subset, $S^{-1}A \to S^{-1}B$ is formally unramified. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
For $S \subset B$ a multiplicative subset, $A \to S^{-1}B$ is formally unramified. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/04E8" data-tag="04E8">10.148.4</a>. (You can also deduce it from Lemma <a href="/tag/00UO" data-tag="00UO">10.148.3</a> combined with Lemma <a href="/tag/00RT" data-tag="00RT">10.131.8</a>.) 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>